"1. The plan treats the merge as moving identity from the chat message to the Artifact row. It gets there by strangler migration: every release has a flag, a metric and a rollback, and none can lose user work or send an installed build a shape it can't decode.\n2. Re-reading the native code found three hard limits for installed Mac 1.6.0 and iPhone builds (N0):\n   - `NativeArtifactStore` fails the whole library on an empty `conversationId`, an unknown kind or a row over 200k characters.\n   - `NativeSyncAPIClient` stops all syncing on any unknown entity type.\n   - Extra JSON keys are ignored, so adding optional fields is safe.\n3. Three mechanisms keep the server inside those limits:\n   - **Anchors:** a deleted chat, or a hand-made design's holder chat, becomes a hidden `kind:\"anchor\"` conversation, so `conversationId` is never null.\n   - **Profiles:** Doc, Deck and Design System are profiles on existing types (MARKDOWN and DESIGN). No new enum values or DesignDocument fields are added until bridge v2.\n   - **Capability headers:** sync output depends on what each client declares; a client with no header gets the legacy shape.\n4. Phase 0A (W1\u2013W2) stops the losses:\n   - deploy `7243613f` (X-03, X-04), fix X-02, check size after expansion (X-08);\n   - conversation delete keeps artifacts instead of cascading (X-22);\n   - a deletion ledger alerts on any hard delete without a stated reason;\n   - owner-only previews move to a separate origin (X-01a); public pages stay static;\n   - designs show as server-rendered SVG pictures instead of JSON (X-20);\n   - an incomplete version never becomes current (X-07);\n   - a server-side save merge restores `cornerSmoothing` for every installed build (X-14);\n   - the telemetry spine goes in.\n5. Phase 0B (W2\u2013W4):\n   - **N1 native release**, cut from main and not tied to the glass ship date: tolerant decoding, client and capability headers, feature flags from `bootstrap.featureFlags`, a CI-gated editor bundle (X-17 to X-19), X-15/X-16 fixes, and iPhone design editing read-only until saves are safe.\n   - **Governance G1:** reversible suspension, takedown, report link, rate limits. Scripted public previews (X-01b) ship only after G1.\n6. Phase 1 (W4\u2013W8) decouples artifacts from messages: `userId`, `projectId`, soft delete with Recently deleted, version provenance, a working head that seals before Juno reads, pinned share versions, a payload diet (p95 \u2264 1.5 MB) and thumbnails on seal (R-004 to R-006, R-014).\n7. Phase 2 (W8\u2013W11) adds `/a/{id}` and one `ArtifactSurface` (card, panel, full window, shared page, phone). Hosts mount by artifact id and adopt new versions in place. Entry points and redirects move one at a time.\n8. Phase 3 (W11\u2013W15) merges the navigation behind `ia.merged`:\n   - one Artifacts index built on the `/library` list code, with type chips, a New menu and trash;\n   - the Design row becomes a pointer for one release, then goes; `/design` redirects with a 308;\n   - Work deliverables and generated images are listed by reference;\n   - the Mac changes land in the glass branch's Phase 4 rather than fighting it.\n9. Phase 4 (W14\u2013W22) is the AI editing loop, per kind and gated on a golden eval set. The model reads the current version and edits by patch or design operations with compare-and-swap; the person's edits win. Every change is a proposal card in the transcript, and Ask Juno becomes a turn in that same conversation.\n10. Phase 5 is parity: comments table, people grants, version stepper and branches, the three typed kinds, bridge v2, then the phone contract and Play. Phase 6 contracts the schema (nullable `conversationId`, anchors dropped) only after N1 reaches \u226595% of Mac and \u226590% of iPhone devices over 14 days, at least 45 days after N1.\n11. Work deliverables: index now (option A) and persist the spec. Documents and presentations fold into Doc and Deck later; spreadsheets, sites and archives stay deliverables. X-25 to X-29 are fixed independently of the merge.\n12. Motion uses existing tokens only. Animation never decides view identity (the cause of X-02); the card-to-panel morph runs on `spring.layout`; Juno's own edits get a one-shot outline fade on `duration-emphasis`; skeletons appear only after 500 ms. On Mac, glass stays on chrome and the dock is opaque.\n13. Section 13 lists what must not ship before what (governance before public scripts, bridge v2 before any DesignDocument field, thumbnails before the navigation merge), plus a 30-flag registry with removal dates and rollback per phase.\n14. Seventeen owner decisions are listed with recommendations. Recommended answers: keep Library and Artifacts as siblings with Design as a type; published links frozen at a version, live links only for invited people; comments in their own table; iPhone design read-only until bridge v2.\n15. The proposal also covers the object model and kind registry, Prisma changes with backfills, routes, creation, sharing, performance and 14 risks, with seven ASCII wireframes.\n\nFiles:\n- /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-liammagnier-Developer-project-juno/bfdee244-0283-4629-a3f4-3c603fc89908/scratchpad/merge/proposal-risk-first.md\n- /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-liammagnier-Developer-project-juno/bfdee244-0283-4629-a3f4-3c603fc89908/scratchpad/merge/_p1.txt (scratch copy of selected backlog items)"